WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:56.100
<b>Vearth</b>

3
00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:56.910
Yahoo!

4
00:01:56.990 --> 00:01:59.620
Good god! Thank you!

5
00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:01.200
I can't believe after
all the suffering

6
00:02:01.290 --> 00:02:02.910
we've endured to find sky island

7
00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:05.410
that it turns out to
be the City of Gold!

8
00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:07.000
Which must be your
way to reward me

9
00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:09.130
for my good behavior,
right, God?

10
00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:11.380
You're just great!

11
00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:12.250
Shut up.

12
00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:13.460
Ten minutes ago you were scared

13
00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:15.810
this God was gonna
kill you, remember?

14
00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:17.310
Well, call me shallow,

15
00:02:17.390 --> 00:02:18.600
but I don't care
how scared I get

16
00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:21.810
as long somebody has
gold waiting for me.

17
00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:23.940
So do you fear or
praise this God?

18
00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:25.400
I'm confused.

19
00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:28.570
All right, I'm done keepin'
up with your mood swings.

20
00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:49.970
Useless!

21
00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:00.580
What is this?

22
00:03:00.850 --> 00:03:02.390
My money says that this is

23
00:03:02.470 --> 00:03:04.440
where we're supposed to
find the next ordeal.

24
00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:07.230
Which means another priest,
so you two, stay awake.

25
00:03:07.310 --> 00:03:08.690
Oh, no.

26
00:03:08.770 --> 00:03:11.780
I think one ordeal is enough
of a nightmare for today.

27
00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:13.490
Which one seems like
it could be out here?

28
00:03:13.570 --> 00:03:15.200
String? Iron? Swamp?

29
00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:16.410
I'm so nervous!

30
00:03:16.490 --> 00:03:18.490
Relax. It's just a grassy field.

31
00:03:18.570 --> 00:03:20.410
Open your eyes!
It's not just a field!

32
00:03:20.490 --> 00:03:22.410
It's a field with a
thousand impaled skulls

33
00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:25.320
set out like trophies to
scare us and it's working!

34
00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:26.360
Yeah, you're right.

35
00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:27.570
I wonder who did this?

36
00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:31.840
Hey, what's that smoke?

37
00:03:32.490 --> 00:03:34.000
We're dead!

38
00:03:47.930 --> 00:03:51.260
Gum-Gum...

39
00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:53.430
...Balloon!

40
00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:01.020
What's wrong with that guy?

41
00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:01.790
Paramythia.

42
00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:03.830
Wyper. We fighting?

43
00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:06.250
Not now. Keep moving.

44
00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:07.720
You.

45
00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:09.680
We're ready! Come on down!

46
00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:11.350
We'll cream you!

47
00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:14.020
Make your move, big guy!

48
00:04:15.810 --> 00:04:18.520
You sound and stink
like Blue Sea People.

49
00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:19.770
Which means you're the ones

50
00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:22.730
causing all the
chaos in Skypiea.

51
00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:24.190
Luffy.

52
00:04:24.270 --> 00:04:26.860
That's the guerilla we saw
back on the White Sea. Look.

53
00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:29.410
What got into him?

54
00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:32.540
There's a guy runnin'
around out there.

55
00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:34.200
Hey, stop! What do you want?

56
00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:35.620
To destroy you!

57
00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:40.720
Just blow us
up and get it over with!

58
00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:42.060
If you don't want to die,

59
00:04:42.140 --> 00:04:44.850
then go back to your
Blue Sea immediately.

60
00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:47.100
Because I promise if
you do anything stupid

61
00:04:47.190 --> 00:04:48.690
on this island...

62
00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:52.440
...we'll execute you with Eneru.

63
00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:56.200
They're up here
trying to kill this guy Eneru?

64
00:04:56.320 --> 00:05:00.150
Then that means that these
guerillas are different.

65
00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:01.780
If different means
they're not priests

66
00:05:01.930 --> 00:05:03.390
then that means they
don't have to kill us!

67
00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:05.710
So for the sake of keeping all
of our body parts attached,

68
00:05:05.830 --> 00:05:07.540
can we please sail on?

69
00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:08.870
Not a chance!

70
00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:11.940
What do you say to a fair
fight, just you and me?

71
00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:14.900
I'm begging you! Please stop!

72
00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:16.750
You stay on that tree branch!

73
00:05:16.840 --> 00:05:18.130
– I'm comin' to you!

74
00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:20.470
– Usopp get off me!

75
00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:22.970
Hands off! I'm trying
to fight here!

76
00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:25.550
Uphold our honor!
I have to! We're pirates!

77
00:05:25.640 --> 00:05:27.470
On second thought.

78
00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:30.270
You'll probably end up
killing each other

79
00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:33.480
before you even have a chance
to make it off this island.

80
00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:40.180
I wonder why they're up here.

81
00:05:40.260 --> 00:05:41.430
I'm not sure.

82
00:05:41.510 --> 00:05:43.550
Must be pretty serious.

83
00:05:43.640 --> 00:05:46.720
But they seem to be enemies
of Eneru as well as us.

84
00:05:46.810 --> 00:05:50.850
You know... I really
do hate this place.

85
00:05:50.940 --> 00:05:52.360
Let's keep moving.

86
00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:08.260
I'll cover you!

87
00:06:09.630 --> 00:06:11.500
Get him outta
that thing's mouth!

88
00:06:13.420 --> 00:06:14.380
Move in now!

89
00:06:55.900 --> 00:06:58.070
We've been
sailing forever, Sanji.

90
00:06:58.150 --> 00:07:00.070
When can we stop?

91
00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:02.360
Can we stop now?

92
00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:03.060
Soon. I just want to make sure

93
00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:04.200
The sun's going down.

94
00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:07.170
I wonder what we'll
run into after dark.

95
00:07:07.250 --> 00:07:10.130
Do you think we can make it
to the altar before then?

96
00:07:10.210 --> 00:07:12.000
No. I don't.

97
00:07:13.130 --> 00:07:15.630
I can barely see the sunset
through those clouds.

98
00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:18.850
I'm surprised they even
have sunsets up here.

99
00:07:31.630 --> 00:07:33.550
Wyper! We can handle these guys!

100
00:07:36.340 --> 00:07:37.550
Yeah, help the others!

101
00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:38.480
Got it!

102
00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:54.870
Chopper!

103
00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:56.620
Where are you, Chopper?

104
00:07:57.510 --> 00:07:59.640
If you can hear me, answer!

105
00:07:59.720 --> 00:08:01.430
Are you there?

106
00:08:01.520 --> 00:08:04.480
Look, her mast is gone
and a wing is ripped in half.

107
00:08:04.560 --> 00:08:06.150
What's he done to
her since we left?

108
00:08:06.230 --> 00:08:08.320
Obviously the
Going Merry was attacked!

109
00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:10.070
Chopper couldn't have
done that to her!

110
00:08:10.150 --> 00:08:11.230
Chopper!

111
00:08:11.330 --> 00:08:13.290
I'm sorry we took so long!

112
00:08:13.370 --> 00:08:15.580
You can come out now,
you'll be safe!

113
00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:17.280
I promise!

114
00:08:17.370 --> 00:08:20.450
At least give us a sign
that you're not dead!

115
00:08:21.790 --> 00:08:24.120
So I guess that means
that he's dead.

116
00:08:24.210 --> 00:08:25.920
Would it kill you
to think positive?

117
00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:28.110
Hey, Chopper!

118
00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:29.160
Come out!

119
00:08:29.240 --> 00:08:30.780
Cause Nami's scared!

120
00:08:30.870 --> 00:08:32.580
And I'm tired!

121
00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:35.910
Hi.

122
00:08:37.790 --> 00:08:38.540
Uh...

123
00:08:40.420 --> 00:08:43.960
Everything stayed ship
shape while you were gone.

124
00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:47.170
You don't have
to lie to us Chopper.

125
00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:49.720
Be strong! Tell us
everything that happened!

126
00:08:53.190 --> 00:08:54.900
...Gatling!

127
00:09:05.230 --> 00:09:07.280
We're soaking wet!

128
00:09:07.620 --> 00:09:09.870
Check it out!

129
00:09:09.950 --> 00:09:11.410
We found it!

130
00:09:11.500 --> 00:09:14.170
There's the altar with the Going
Merry sitting right on top.

131
00:09:14.250 --> 00:09:15.960
– Huh?
– Huh?

132
00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:19.550
Nami! Robin!

133
00:09:19.580 --> 00:09:21.660
I missed you so much!

134
00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:22.890
Sorry to keep you waiting,

135
00:09:22.970 --> 00:09:25.390
but I beat the ordeal
of love to get here!

136
00:09:25.470 --> 00:09:27.850
I thought it
was spheres, not love.

137
00:09:27.930 --> 00:09:28.930
If that was love,

138
00:09:29.020 --> 00:09:30.520
I don't ever want
to find it again.

139
00:09:30.600 --> 00:09:31.980
Anyway, who cares!

140
00:09:32.060 --> 00:09:33.690
– We're alive! We're alive!

141
00:09:33.770 --> 00:09:35.650
Sounds like they're
happy to be here.

142
00:09:35.730 --> 00:09:38.110
Safe and sound.

143
00:09:45.090 --> 00:09:47.670
Where's the... mast?

144
00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:50.420
Uh, look. I tried,

145
00:09:50.510 --> 00:09:52.220
but it didn't matter
how hard I fought.

146
00:09:52.300 --> 00:09:54.600
He still kept
burning everything.

147
00:09:54.680 --> 00:09:56.600
I promise I did
everything I could.

148
00:09:56.680 --> 00:09:59.060
Yeah, well are you
gonna be okay or what?

149
00:10:00.920 --> 00:10:02.840
Mm-hmm.

150
00:10:04.300 --> 00:10:06.720
You must've been scared
facing that guy by yourself.

151
00:10:06.800 --> 00:10:08.510
It's a good thing he
set the mast on fire

152
00:10:08.590 --> 00:10:10.890
instead of you, right?

153
00:10:10.970 --> 00:10:14.220
We can figure out the details
on the ship later.

154
00:10:14.650 --> 00:10:16.820
I promise to become
a more dependable man

155
00:10:18.410 --> 00:10:19.830
starting right now!

156
00:10:19.910 --> 00:10:22.580
Chopper, stop yelling at the
altar and tell me something.

157
00:10:22.660 --> 00:10:25.120
How'd you get rid
of that priest?

158
00:10:25.210 --> 00:10:27.040
I used the whistle
the Sky Knight gave us

159
00:10:27.130 --> 00:10:28.790
and he showed up to rescue me.

160
00:10:28.880 --> 00:10:30.090
Oh. Where is he?

161
00:10:30.170 --> 00:10:31.710
I don't see him.

162
00:10:42.230 --> 00:10:45.110
He's willing to sacrifice
this much for us

163
00:10:45.170 --> 00:10:47.790
even though he gave us
that whistle for free.

164
00:10:48.610 --> 00:10:49.860
If it wasn't for the Sky Knight,

165
00:10:49.950 --> 00:10:51.490
you guys probably
wouldn't have a ship

166
00:10:51.570 --> 00:10:53.240
and I'd for sure be dead.

167
00:10:53.320 --> 00:10:55.580
I got a bunch of
questions for him,

168
00:10:55.660 --> 00:10:57.950
but I guess I'll wait
till he wakes up.

169
00:10:58.040 --> 00:11:00.120
We owe you a thanks as well.

170
00:11:04.060 --> 00:11:05.390
Luffy!

171
00:11:07.550 --> 00:11:10.050
The Going Merry's trashed
and it'll be dark soon,

172
00:11:10.140 --> 00:11:11.260
so there's no chance
we'll make it

173
00:11:11.350 --> 00:11:13.850
back to Angel Island
until tomorrow.

174
00:11:14.890 --> 00:11:16.020
We should hop over to the land

175
00:11:16.100 --> 00:11:17.940
and make camp on
shore for the night.

176
00:11:18.020 --> 00:11:19.440
Hm? Why there?

177
00:11:19.520 --> 00:11:21.400
Because if we stay here
and someone attacks us,

178
00:11:21.480 --> 00:11:23.570
the first thing to take a
beating will be our ship.

179
00:11:23.650 --> 00:11:25.900
Would you use your head, Luffy?

180
00:11:25.970 --> 00:11:28.010
Not to mention it's
easier to fight from land

181
00:11:28.100 --> 00:11:30.100
than from an altar
floating on a cloud.

182
00:11:33.350 --> 00:11:34.480
Camping!

183
00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:35.650
This isn't a party!

184
00:11:35.730 --> 00:11:37.360
We're in enemy territory!

185
00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:38.560
Now calm down!

186
00:11:38.650 --> 00:11:40.440
Not a party. Got it.

187
00:11:41.450 --> 00:11:43.700
It was shot into
the sky like us.

188
00:11:47.290 --> 00:11:49.210
Excellent work!

189
00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:51.940
<b>The priests can predict our attacks using mantra!</b>

190
00:11:49.290 --> 00:11:51.040
Now, based on your reports,

191
00:11:51.120 --> 00:11:53.920
we've learned that the priests
can predict our movements

192
00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:56.170
using a power they
like to call Mantra.

193
00:11:56.200 --> 00:12:01.120
<b>The bird blows flames! The spear burns you!</b>

194
00:11:56.200 --> 00:12:00.410
<b>The part of Jaya we thought had sunk
was actually in the sky! in the sky!</b>

195
00:11:56.250 --> 00:11:58.590
And the bird blows flames
and the spear burns you.

196
00:11:58.670 --> 00:12:01.180
But most importantly
we've learned this:

197
00:12:00.410 --> 00:12:01.120
<b>The part of Jaya we thought had sunk
was actually in the sky! in the sky!</b>

198
00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:06.870
<b>The priests can predict our attacks using mantra!</b>
<b>The bird blows flames! The spear burns you!</b>
<b>The part of Jaya we thought had sunk
was actually in the sky!</b>

199
00:12:01.210 --> 00:12:03.710
The City of Gold is not a
thousand leagues under the sea

200
00:12:03.820 --> 00:12:04.820
as we had thought, but it is

201
00:12:04.910 --> 00:12:07.030
hidden somewhere
on this very island.

202
00:12:07.090 --> 00:12:08.760
No way!

203
00:12:08.840 --> 00:12:10.970
That was the first
thing I told you!

204
00:12:11.090 --> 00:12:13.920
So, what is this Mantra
business all about?

205
00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:17.090
Maybe it's some kind of sixth
sense you only get up here.

206
00:12:17.150 --> 00:12:18.700
Sixth sense?

207
00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:21.550
Yo, Chopper, do I need to
grind this down any more?

208
00:12:21.620 --> 00:12:24.080
Yes. It needs
to be a fine powder.

209
00:12:24.160 --> 00:12:27.620
He's suffered a lot of damage
to his digestive system.

210
00:12:31.540 --> 00:12:32.840
This is it!

211
00:12:32.840 --> 00:12:35.010
An adventure with
gold at the end!

212
00:12:35.050 --> 00:12:37.470
I can't wait!

213
00:12:37.550 --> 00:12:39.880
Glad to see someone
on my side. I'm ready.

214
00:12:39.780 --> 00:12:44.160
<b>The priests can predict our attacks using mantra!</b>

215
00:12:40.010 --> 00:12:41.180
Luffy, no.

216
00:12:41.260 --> 00:12:42.930
Did you forget what that
scary guerilla guy said

217
00:12:43.010 --> 00:12:45.140
about execution?

218
00:12:45.230 --> 00:12:47.600
God will be really mad.

219
00:12:49.330 --> 00:12:50.900
Sounds like fun.

220
00:12:50.900 --> 00:12:52.900
Well, we wouldn't be
very good pirates

221
00:12:52.920 --> 00:12:54.630
if we turned our backs on gold.

222
00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:56.040
So let's not.

223
00:12:56.100 --> 00:12:57.310
It won't be easy.

224
00:12:57.400 --> 00:13:00.480
You know everybody up
here already hates us.

225
00:13:00.570 --> 00:13:02.030
Which means I'm in.

226
00:13:02.100 --> 00:13:03.680
Come on.

227
00:13:05.060 --> 00:13:07.940
Aren't you even a little
frightened of the wrath of God?

228
00:13:08.020 --> 00:13:11.020
I mean, I wanna live! Don't you?

229
00:13:19.610 --> 00:13:20.530
Gold!

230
00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:23.700
And it's all waitin' for us!

231
00:13:25.670 --> 00:13:27.760
Kamakiri, you've gotta move!

232
00:13:29.870 --> 00:13:31.790
Thanks, I owe you
one after that Kamakiri.

233
00:13:33.260 --> 00:13:34.430
Ah!

234
00:13:34.510 --> 00:13:35.850
Kamakiri!

235
00:13:35.930 --> 00:13:37.180
Ah!

236
00:13:42.230 --> 00:13:44.400
Wyper! Kamakiri's taken a hit!

237
00:13:44.480 --> 00:13:46.150
Huh? What happened?

238
00:13:50.780 --> 00:13:54.330
Damn. So close to victory.

239
00:13:54.410 --> 00:13:58.160
Heh! But you never
even had a chance.

240
00:13:58.280 --> 00:14:01.990
When night falls, we'll have
an even greater advantage.

241
00:14:10.850 --> 00:14:12.350
We're moving out!

242
00:14:12.440 --> 00:14:14.520
Grab all our wounded and meet
back at the rendezvous point!

243
00:14:14.600 --> 00:14:15.900
Now!

244
00:14:17.820 --> 00:14:20.230
You're not getting away!

245
00:14:20.320 --> 00:14:23.280
Ohm, wait.

246
00:14:23.550 --> 00:14:24.720
What is it?

247
00:14:25.780 --> 00:14:28.370
We have been summoned
by God Eneru.

248
00:14:38.380 --> 00:14:39.500
Hmm?

249
00:14:40.630 --> 00:14:42.300
Why'd you stop?

250
00:14:43.280 --> 00:14:45.240
Ah! Boring!

251
00:14:45.750 --> 00:14:48.550
Nobody told you
to watch the boiling water.

252
00:14:48.630 --> 00:14:50.550
You have one job
and one job only.

253
00:14:50.630 --> 00:14:53.640
Take the distilled water
and fill up the canteens,

254
00:14:53.720 --> 00:14:55.390
so make sure that happens.

255
00:14:55.390 --> 00:14:58.770
We'll need fresh
drinking water tomorrow.

256
00:14:58.850 --> 00:15:01.430
Hmph. Whatever.

257
00:15:01.520 --> 00:15:03.520
Sanji, we found
tons of great stuff.

258
00:15:03.600 --> 00:15:06.020
Excellent. Let's see the haul.

259
00:15:06.100 --> 00:15:08.650
We found walnuts,
aloe, bananas, garlic.

260
00:15:08.680 --> 00:15:09.850
Rats and frogs, too.

261
00:15:09.980 --> 00:15:11.900
Nice. It all goes in the pot.

262
00:15:11.980 --> 00:15:13.190
Disgusting!

263
00:15:13.280 --> 00:15:15.030
You don't expect us
to eat that mess, do you?!

264
00:15:15.110 --> 00:15:16.660
Oh, silly me.

265
00:15:16.740 --> 00:15:19.820
Nami, I promise,
I'l take the garlic out.

266
00:15:19.940 --> 00:15:21.780
The garlic's
the only good thing!

267
00:15:21.860 --> 00:15:25.410
Is our navigator
having another meltdown?

268
00:15:25.490 --> 00:15:27.740
Now that's what I call a gem.

269
00:15:27.840 --> 00:15:29.100
It's huge!

270
00:15:29.170 --> 00:15:32.250
Big, yes,
but it's not a gemstone.

271
00:15:32.350 --> 00:15:34.520
Hey, that's a big salt crystal.

272
00:15:34.600 --> 00:15:36.980
Nice find, Robin dear.

273
00:15:37.060 --> 00:15:38.730
I found it on the shore.

274
00:15:38.810 --> 00:15:40.980
And I figured we'd
find some use for it.

275
00:15:41.070 --> 00:15:42.980
Not only is salt
vital to survival,

276
00:15:43.090 --> 00:15:45.340
but without it, my food
would taste awful!

277
00:15:47.060 --> 00:15:49.430
If I take half of
the garlic and aloe,

278
00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:52.220
then I can make antiseptic
and burn ointment

279
00:15:52.320 --> 00:15:53.900
and use it to heal
the Sky Knight.

280
00:15:53.990 --> 00:15:56.030
Yeah? You need any frog?

281
00:15:56.100 --> 00:15:57.190
No. No frog.

282
00:15:57.270 --> 00:15:58.810
Zoro, you're not doing anything.

283
00:15:58.910 --> 00:16:02.120
I got a little job for you.

284
00:16:03.940 --> 00:16:08.160
Sanji, my swords were not
meant to be used like this.

285
00:16:08.270 --> 00:16:11.150
Yeah, but disobey the
chef and you probably won't eat.

286
00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:12.450
So it's your call.

287
00:16:16.360 --> 00:16:18.530
Ah! You just
dropped a rock in the stew!

288
00:16:18.610 --> 00:16:20.610
– Is it good?
– We don't eat it.

289
00:16:20.700 --> 00:16:22.160
It helps the pot cook.

290
00:16:22.180 --> 00:16:25.020
The stone's heat cooks
the stew from the inside out.

291
00:16:25.100 --> 00:16:26.060
Ah...

292
00:16:26.180 --> 00:16:27.680
Trust me on this one.

293
00:16:27.730 --> 00:16:30.730
You'll need all the nutrients in
this dish to survive this place.

294
00:16:30.810 --> 00:16:31.940
Perfect, then.

295
00:16:32.060 --> 00:16:33.650
Smells like we got a winner...

296
00:16:34.770 --> 00:16:36.110
Keep your hands off!

297
00:16:37.060 --> 00:16:39.810
Sanji. I'm hungry.

298
00:16:39.820 --> 00:16:41.490
Well, it's not ready yet!

299
00:16:41.590 --> 00:16:43.260
Weren't you just
cramming a skyshark

300
00:16:43.340 --> 00:16:45.760
down your gullet not
ten minutes ago?

301
00:16:45.850 --> 00:16:48.470
Yeah. But that
was just an appetizer.

302
00:16:48.560 --> 00:16:49.730
I figured you knew that.

303
00:16:49.830 --> 00:16:52.290
He must have
a rubber stomach, too.

304
00:16:52.490 --> 00:16:54.200
Yeah, tell me about it.

305
00:16:57.280 --> 00:16:58.370
What are you doing Usopp?

306
00:16:58.450 --> 00:17:00.700
Sanji's almost got
dinner laid out for us.

307
00:17:00.750 --> 00:17:03.590
I figured, since
I wasn't doing anything anyway,

308
00:17:03.670 --> 00:17:07.090
I'd start hauling this wood
over to the ship for repairs.

309
00:17:07.190 --> 00:17:08.780
You're gonna
swim over there, huh?

310
00:17:08.880 --> 00:17:10.170
Yeah.

311
00:17:10.240 --> 00:17:12.860
So you don't have a
problem with the giant sharks?

312
00:17:17.420 --> 00:17:18.920
The ship will
still be broken tomorrow,

313
00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:21.330
I'll fix it then.
Let's eat, Zoro!

314
00:17:23.330 --> 00:17:24.710
What a moron.

315
00:17:28.130 --> 00:17:29.720
Yes! Finished!

316
00:17:29.800 --> 00:17:32.130
Soup's on,
but it's ladies first. Got it?

317
00:17:32.220 --> 00:17:33.390
Sure.

318
00:17:33.500 --> 00:17:34.670
If you would all
please take your seats,

319
00:17:34.760 --> 00:17:36.430
I'll be around with
your meals shortly.

320
00:17:36.510 --> 00:17:38.470
And eat up... I don't
want it getting cold.

321
00:17:38.560 --> 00:17:40.480
Now, if you would all
listen up while you eat,

322
00:17:40.560 --> 00:17:42.940
I'll explain how we're going
to handle this tomorrow.

323
00:17:43.380 --> 00:17:45.380
Oohh, it looks tasty!

324
00:17:46.190 --> 00:17:49.280
Anyway... Let's review
Noland's book first.

325
00:17:49.360 --> 00:17:52.240
He discovered the
City of Gold 400 years ago.

326
00:17:52.320 --> 00:17:54.280
However, after leaving the
island and returning with

327
00:17:54.360 --> 00:17:57.080
his king, he found the
gold ruins had vanished.

328
00:17:57.160 --> 00:17:59.910
Luckily, we now know what
happened to these ruins.

329
00:17:59.990 --> 00:18:02.750
Keep the ladle handy,
I'll be back for more after I...

330
00:18:03.970 --> 00:18:05.930
Sanji, pay attention!

331
00:18:06.010 --> 00:18:08.060
I was, but he
was interrupting you!

332
00:18:08.140 --> 00:18:10.730
I compliment his food
and this is the thanks I get?

333
00:18:10.810 --> 00:18:11.890
Sheesh!

334
00:18:11.910 --> 00:18:14.500
The point I was getting at

335
00:18:14.610 --> 00:18:15.860
is that the gold didn't sink

336
00:18:15.950 --> 00:18:18.120
into the ocean, but was
shot up here into the sky

337
00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:21.410
by the knock-up stream
just like we were.

338
00:18:21.490 --> 00:18:23.000
Do you really
think a whole island

339
00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:24.620
could have done that?

340
00:18:24.670 --> 00:18:26.920
Well, it's the only
thing that makes sense.

341
00:18:27.010 --> 00:18:28.680
Remember? Cricket
said that every time

342
00:18:28.760 --> 00:18:31.640
this phenomenon occurs it's
in a different location.

343
00:18:31.720 --> 00:18:33.510
Yeah, that explosion
was enormous.

344
00:18:33.630 --> 00:18:35.670
I'm not surprised
it lifted an island.

345
00:18:35.760 --> 00:18:38.800
Hmm. It's just hard
to believe that the forest

346
00:18:38.840 --> 00:18:42.140
we're sitting in is the same
one we saw back on Jaya.

347
00:18:42.220 --> 00:18:43.850
I believe that
has something to do with

348
00:18:43.930 --> 00:18:46.850
the odd composition of
the island clouds up here.

349
00:18:46.930 --> 00:18:49.190
Look at all the trees,
fish, and wildlife.

350
00:18:49.270 --> 00:18:51.020
Something about this
environment dramatically

351
00:18:51.110 --> 00:18:52.940
increases growth rates.

352
00:18:53.020 --> 00:18:54.940
Which explains how
a society here could have been

353
00:18:55.030 --> 00:18:56.770
swallowed up by these
burgeoning forces.

354
00:18:56.770 --> 00:18:58.480
That also explains
why the South Birds

355
00:18:58.560 --> 00:19:01.980
who saved us were so huge.
I couldn't believe it.

356
00:19:02.070 --> 00:19:05.240
Yeah, 400 years of
growing will do that to a bird.

357
00:19:05.320 --> 00:19:07.990
Then why... Here.
Why did those South Birds

358
00:19:08.070 --> 00:19:10.910
go to such great lengths
to save you guys?

359
00:19:10.990 --> 00:19:13.240
Um... I don't know.

360
00:19:13.300 --> 00:19:15.720
But, when they saw him,
they referred to

361
00:19:15.800 --> 00:19:18.550
– the Sky Knight as God.

362
00:19:18.670 --> 00:19:20.960
He's god? So if we
beat the crud out of this guy,

363
00:19:21.040 --> 00:19:22.340
then our job here is done!

364
00:19:22.390 --> 00:19:23.560
No, genius!

365
00:19:23.700 --> 00:19:25.040
How did you get that out
of what he's saying?!

366
00:19:25.120 --> 00:19:27.500
Would both of you
loudmouths just pipe down?!

367
00:19:27.810 --> 00:19:28.770
Yeah, shut up!

368
00:19:28.770 --> 00:19:30.230
Yeah. Wait, who's a loudmouth?

369
00:19:30.250 --> 00:19:33.010
– You are!
– You both are. Can it.

370
00:19:33.090 --> 00:19:35.260
Now does anyone recall
what Noland's log said

371
00:19:35.310 --> 00:19:36.650
about the City of Gold?

372
00:19:36.670 --> 00:19:38.760
I do! It's a city of gold!

373
00:19:38.840 --> 00:19:39.840
You're such a dumbass!

374
00:19:39.920 --> 00:19:41.840
Do you ever think
before you talk?!

375
00:19:41.910 --> 00:19:43.450
I think he wrote
about South Birds

376
00:19:43.550 --> 00:19:45.390
and a giant gold bell.

377
00:19:45.470 --> 00:19:47.720
'Course there
could be a lot more.

378
00:19:47.790 --> 00:19:49.420
The last thing
he wrote in the log before

379
00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:51.500
he died was something odd.

380
00:19:51.530 --> 00:19:53.030
It's something
I can't figure out

381
00:19:53.110 --> 00:19:54.910
even after seeing this island.

382
00:19:55.300 --> 00:19:57.720
It says "The City of Gold
is in a skull's right eye."

383
00:19:57.740 --> 00:20:00.160
That's it! Check it out.

384
00:20:00.250 --> 00:20:03.470
I matched up Robin's map of
Jaya with the old Skypiea map

385
00:20:03.550 --> 00:20:05.510
that we found in the shipwreck.

386
00:20:05.650 --> 00:20:07.410
Of course, this isn't
exact and there may be

387
00:20:07.490 --> 00:20:10.030
some incorrect overlap, but
when you match up the location

388
00:20:10.130 --> 00:20:13.590
of Cricket's house with the
broken part we found up here,

389
00:20:13.670 --> 00:20:17.340
this is what Jaya looked
like 400 years ago.

390
00:20:17.430 --> 00:20:18.970
Neat! It's a skull!

391
00:20:19.160 --> 00:20:20.740
It is a skull!

392
00:20:22.160 --> 00:20:23.080
Well?

393
00:20:24.210 --> 00:20:25.830
Way to go, Nami!

394
00:20:25.910 --> 00:20:27.540
We did it!

395
00:20:28.670 --> 00:20:30.750
Okay. But where
in the skull's right eye?

396
00:20:32.250 --> 00:20:33.380
Hmm...
I'm thinking right here.

397
00:20:34.050 --> 00:20:37.470
It's the one structure
that's actually inside the eye.

398
00:20:37.550 --> 00:20:39.720
And no one's found it yet
because of all the people

399
00:20:39.800 --> 00:20:43.020
who have tried, we're the
ones who had both maps.

400
00:20:43.100 --> 00:20:47.440
Ah. Of course.
We must be lucky pirates.

401
00:20:47.520 --> 00:20:48.770
It kinda makes sense.

402
00:20:48.980 --> 00:20:50.350
Hidden treasure!

403
00:20:50.350 --> 00:20:51.860
Treasure!

404
00:20:52.230 --> 00:20:53.850
The only thing left
to do is make our way

405
00:20:53.940 --> 00:20:55.480
to the skull's eye.

406
00:20:55.560 --> 00:20:57.520
But since we can't
leave the ship unguarded,

407
00:20:57.610 --> 00:21:00.320
tomorrow morning, we'll split
the crew into two teams.

408
00:21:01.610 --> 00:21:02.940
This is our time.

409
00:21:03.030 --> 00:21:05.110
On the other side of
this island waits more gold

410
00:21:05.200 --> 00:21:06.820
than we've ever dreamed.

411
00:21:07.440 --> 00:21:11.160
Now that's what I call gourmet!

412
00:21:11.240 --> 00:21:12.610
Tomorrow, we get the gold!

413
00:21:12.700 --> 00:21:14.990
You got it!

414
00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:16.960
You think it'll be sunny again?

415
00:21:16.960 --> 00:21:18.670
We are above the clouds
so I'd guess "yes."

416
00:21:19.040 --> 00:21:21.000
Let's put out the fires
if we don't need them.

417
00:21:21.070 --> 00:21:23.400
It's beginning
to get late, you guys.

418
00:21:23.500 --> 00:21:24.790
We don't want
to announce our location

419
00:21:24.860 --> 00:21:26.070
to our enemies.

420
00:21:26.160 --> 00:21:28.370
Hmph. What a rookie move.

421
00:21:28.390 --> 00:21:29.770
You hear that Usopp?

422
00:21:29.870 --> 00:21:32.910
She wants us to douse the fire.
What are we gonna do?

423
00:21:33.000 --> 00:21:33.910
Huh?

424
00:21:33.990 --> 00:21:35.030
I don't know.

425
00:21:35.120 --> 00:21:36.870
It's not really
her fault though.

426
00:21:36.930 --> 00:21:39.680
She's never been exposed
to this kind of living before.

427
00:21:39.760 --> 00:21:41.220
We should be tolerant.

428
00:21:41.300 --> 00:21:45.390
Huh?
What are you two saying?

429
00:21:45.470 --> 00:21:47.350
You're always
supposed to have a campfire when

430
00:21:47.420 --> 00:21:49.840
you camp that's what
makes it camping!

431
00:21:49.940 --> 00:21:51.230
'Cause it's
the warmth of the flame

432
00:21:51.310 --> 00:21:53.110
fighting through
all this wilderness

433
00:21:53.190 --> 00:21:55.150
that reminds us
that we're human!

434
00:21:55.230 --> 00:21:57.530
It's never-ending
with those idiots.

435
00:21:57.610 --> 00:21:59.950
Hey! Lay off the sob stories!

436
00:22:00.030 --> 00:22:01.870
You know how dangerous
this island can be.

437
00:22:01.950 --> 00:22:03.780
Let's not give it
any help in killing us.

438
00:22:03.870 --> 00:22:05.030
Don't care.

439
00:22:05.120 --> 00:22:06.790
We're in the middle of
a war between priests

440
00:22:06.870 --> 00:22:09.420
protecting their god and
guerillas forging a coup!

441
00:22:09.510 --> 00:22:11.470
Not to mention the giant,
bloodthirsty monsters

442
00:22:11.540 --> 00:22:13.880
that wait around
every corner to eat us

443
00:22:13.960 --> 00:22:15.260
Not monsters!

444
00:22:15.340 --> 00:22:17.880
Sky island scary.
Sky island scary.

445
00:22:17.960 --> 00:22:20.010
Luffy, take a look!

446
00:22:20.090 --> 00:22:22.220
Is this enough
wood for your fire?

447
00:22:22.300 --> 00:22:24.810
Can you idiots
think for one second?!

448
00:22:24.890 --> 00:22:28.480
Heh. Don't worry.
Wild animals are afraid of fire.

449
00:22:28.560 --> 00:22:30.440
They'll stay away.

450
00:22:30.520 --> 00:22:32.100
But they're surrounding us.

451
00:22:32.190 --> 00:22:34.190
We have to run or we'll die!

452
00:22:41.570 --> 00:22:43.160
Chopper. I think
it's trying to talk.

453
00:22:43.240 --> 00:22:44.450
You mind translating?

454
00:22:49.180 --> 00:22:51.020
♪ We're more than just companions ♪

455
00:22:51.020 --> 00:22:53.180
♪ Beyond what you would call friends ♪

456
00:22:51.280 --> 00:22:54.910
It's the Festival on
the Night Before, Gold-Hunting!

457
00:22:53.180 --> 00:22:56.480
♪ We're each others own FAMILY! ♪

458
00:22:55.560 --> 00:22:57.560
♪ While we're all on the sea ♪

459
00:22:56.480 --> 00:22:58.690
♪ Not one of us are siblings ♪

460
00:22:58.690 --> 00:23:01.190
♪ We don't share any blood ♪

461
00:22:59.290 --> 00:23:01.080
This is fantastic!

462
00:23:01.190 --> 00:23:03.320
And you guys
really make this stuff?

463
00:23:01.570 --> 00:23:05.910
♪ But our crew is still FAMILY! ♪

464
00:23:03.320 --> 00:23:04.990
That's great! More please!

465
00:23:05.290 --> 00:23:07.840
Hmm?

466
00:23:11.290 --> 00:23:14.660
♪ Survey maps galore, ♪

467
00:23:14.660 --> 00:23:19.210
♪ The biggest maps you've ever laid your eyes on ♪

468
00:23:18.930 --> 00:23:20.640
I love you guys.

469
00:23:19.210 --> 00:23:21.920
♪ It wouldn't matter anyway, ♪

470
00:23:20.730 --> 00:23:22.690
Tomorrow the treasure's ours!

471
00:23:21.920 --> 00:23:24.670
♪ You'll never find family like this ♪

472
00:23:22.780 --> 00:23:23.780
Our treasure!

473
00:23:23.860 --> 00:23:25.400
Tomorrow!

474
00:23:24.670 --> 00:23:29.470
♪ Only outstanding slackers and misfits ♪

475
00:23:27.910 --> 00:23:29.530
I'm surprised
you're getting along so well

476
00:23:29.470 --> 00:23:33.100
♪ Can come aboard our MOTHER SHIP ♪

477
00:23:29.630 --> 00:23:32.350
with the cloud wolves.

478
00:23:32.480 --> 00:23:34.020
I know of no one else
who could have such

479
00:23:33.100 --> 00:23:37.020
♪ Forsake all reason, then maybe ♪

480
00:23:34.110 --> 00:23:36.820
raucous festivities
on Eneru's land.

481
00:23:37.020 --> 00:23:41.150
♪ You can sail along with us ♪

482
00:23:37.950 --> 00:23:39.450
It's good to
see that you're awake.

483
00:23:39.530 --> 00:23:40.950
Are you feeling any better?

484
00:23:41.040 --> 00:23:43.540
I apologize for being
such a burden to you all.

485
00:23:42.940 --> 00:23:46.530
♪ EVERYDAY ride out the storm ♪

486
00:23:43.620 --> 00:23:46.420
Hey. You're too hard
on yourself old man.

487
00:23:46.500 --> 00:23:49.250
You saved Chopper, and you
kept our ship from being blown

488
00:23:46.530 --> 00:23:50.280
♪ That's all we can ask for ♪

489
00:23:49.330 --> 00:23:50.590
to a thousand pieces.

490
00:23:50.280 --> 00:23:54.120
♪ We'll find the greatest treasure, it's our quest, ♪

491
00:23:50.670 --> 00:23:51.800
That's my duty.

492
00:23:51.880 --> 00:23:53.130
There's still
plenty of stew left.

493
00:23:53.210 --> 00:23:54.130
Would you like some?

494
00:23:54.120 --> 00:24:00.290
♪ with the aid of our MOTHER SHIP ♪

495
00:23:54.210 --> 00:23:55.300
Thank you, no.

496
00:23:55.380 --> 00:23:56.800
Not right now.

497
00:23:59.800 --> 00:24:03.970
Hey! Thanks for everything,
Sky Knight guy! Let's dance!

498
00:24:01.420 --> 00:24:05.220
♪ The best people share a quirk, yeah ♪

499
00:24:04.060 --> 00:24:05.890
C'mon, dance with us, Gan Fall!

500
00:24:05.220 --> 00:24:11.470
♪ They can laugh like no one else can! ♪

501
00:24:05.990 --> 00:24:07.440
Chopper, you been drinking?!

502
00:24:09.050 --> 00:24:10.880
Hey, old man, I gotta question.

503
00:24:10.970 --> 00:24:12.510
Conis. Is she okay?

504
00:24:12.430 --> 00:24:14.560
♪ We're more than just companions ♪

505
00:24:12.590 --> 00:24:13.720
Very much so.

506
00:24:13.800 --> 00:24:15.930
I've sheltered her and
her father at my house.

507
00:24:14.560 --> 00:24:16.640
♪ Beyond what you would call friends ♪

508
00:24:16.010 --> 00:24:17.390
They're fine.

509
00:24:16.640 --> 00:24:20.060
♪ We're each other's own FAMILY! ♪

510
00:24:17.470 --> 00:24:20.350
Great. I was worried
she'd never see me again.

511
00:24:18.900 --> 00:24:21.860
♪ While there's fun and we're free! ♪

512
00:24:20.060 --> 00:24:22.020
♪ Not one of us are siblings, ♪

513
00:24:20.430 --> 00:24:22.770
I'm so happy that
both of them are safe.

514
00:24:22.020 --> 00:24:25.030
♪ We don't share any blood ♪

515
00:24:22.850 --> 00:24:25.360
Now. Let's celebrate
by tossing Chopper.

516
00:24:25.030 --> 00:24:29.320
♪ But our crew is still FAMILY! ♪

517
00:24:25.440 --> 00:24:26.690
Why me?!

518
00:24:40.680 --> 00:24:42.100
I'm sorry for eavesdropping,

519
00:24:42.180 --> 00:24:44.020
but I heard your earlier
conversation about how

520
00:24:44.130 --> 00:24:47.680
this island was known
long ago by the name Jaya.

521
00:24:47.730 --> 00:24:49.110
Yeah, that's right.

522
00:24:49.190 --> 00:24:51.110
But I believe you
have yet to hear the story

523
00:24:51.190 --> 00:24:53.610
of how this island
on which we sit...

524
00:24:53.700 --> 00:24:56.490
...came to be known
as such holy ground.

525
00:25:04.210 --> 00:25:05.870
Is this what was
so distracting for you

526
00:25:05.960 --> 00:25:07.170
in battle, Laki?

527
00:25:07.260 --> 00:25:08.970
Are you here to sabotage us?

528
00:25:09.060 --> 00:25:11.060
Get in our way and slow us down?

529
00:25:11.140 --> 00:25:15.150
No, I'm not.
I feel awful for Kamakiri.

530
00:25:15.230 --> 00:25:16.900
We were fighting the priests!

531
00:25:16.980 --> 00:25:18.940
We can't afford to be
off task at all if we want

532
00:25:20.280 --> 00:25:22.320
Apologizing won't
fix anything... I know that!

533
00:25:22.410 --> 00:25:24.330
So give that back to me. Now!

534
00:25:24.430 --> 00:25:26.600
It belongs to Aisa! It's hers!

535
00:25:26.660 --> 00:25:28.660
I promised I would bring
back some vearth for her!

536
00:25:28.750 --> 00:25:30.080
Give it back to me! Please!

537
00:25:30.160 --> 00:25:32.290
– Shut up!
– You have to let me have it...

538
00:25:35.540 --> 00:25:39.170
Kamakiri. You shouldn't
even be standing right now.

539
00:25:39.640 --> 00:25:41.600
I can still fight.

540
00:25:44.410 --> 00:25:46.120
You're right about
this being our best time

541
00:25:46.200 --> 00:25:47.870
to strike the Upper Yard.

542
00:25:52.000 --> 00:25:54.000
With Satori gone,
we proved today

543
00:25:54.090 --> 00:25:56.930
that we can defeat
the remaining priests.

544
00:25:57.040 --> 00:25:59.910
I say we attack
again tomorrow, at first light.

545
00:26:08.090 --> 00:26:09.840
The ground of
the Upper Yard must remind

546
00:26:09.920 --> 00:26:12.680
you Blue Sea people
of your home far below.

547
00:26:12.760 --> 00:26:14.260
It is similar, right?

548
00:26:14.350 --> 00:26:16.510
It is.

549
00:26:16.600 --> 00:26:18.970
Yes. You're lucky.

550
00:26:19.060 --> 00:26:21.390
What you see all around us
and beneath our feet

551
00:26:21.640 --> 00:26:24.690
is something that does not
naturally exist in the sky.

552
00:26:25.020 --> 00:26:27.310
Island cloud
can support plant life,

553
00:26:27.360 --> 00:26:29.490
but it cannot generate its own.

554
00:26:29.610 --> 00:26:33.740
Greenery and soil are both
foreign things to our life here.

555
00:26:40.660 --> 00:26:43.040
Our people have
our own name for this.

556
00:26:43.120 --> 00:26:44.540
It's vearth.

557
00:26:46.080 --> 00:26:49.090
Those living among
the clouds hold this sacred.

558
00:26:49.130 --> 00:26:51.180
It's what they all desire.

559
00:26:54.260 --> 00:26:56.050
Once we kill Eneru...

560
00:26:56.140 --> 00:26:57.810
...there will be no need
for you to sneak around

561
00:26:57.890 --> 00:27:01.020
obsessing over a
single bag of vearth.

562
00:27:01.100 --> 00:27:03.810
The time is now.

563
00:27:07.400 --> 00:27:10.190
We will return
after 400 years of exile...

564
00:27:10.280 --> 00:27:13.030
to the true home
of the Shandorians!

565
00:27:13.680 --> 00:27:16.310
Aww, come on, Zoro, be a pal!

566
00:27:16.450 --> 00:27:18.450
Forget it!
I'm not going with you!

567
00:27:18.900 --> 00:27:20.480
If you're scared,
just hold it till morning

568
00:27:20.560 --> 00:27:22.530
and quit whining, you big baby!

569
00:27:22.610 --> 00:27:25.570
I would if I could, believe me!

570
00:27:25.650 --> 00:27:28.240
Just go take a leak by yourself!

571
00:27:28.320 --> 00:27:31.620
That's cold,
Zoro. That's really cold!

572
00:27:51.370 --> 00:27:54.500
– What was that noise?

573
00:28:04.120 --> 00:28:07.210
There shouldn't be anyone
on the ship at this hour.

574
00:28:08.290 --> 00:28:11.580
Jeez, this fog is
so thick I can't see who it is.

575
00:28:41.060 --> 00:28:41.980
Huh?

576
00:28:46.730 --> 00:28:49.360
What's your problem, you moron?

577
00:28:49.440 --> 00:28:51.820
Did you fall asleep mid-piss?

578
00:28:51.900 --> 00:28:54.610
That's pathetic.

579
00:28:54.700 --> 00:28:57.070
I... I...

580
00:28:57.160 --> 00:28:58.910
I saw... I...

581
00:28:58.990 --> 00:29:01.540
Hey, Usopp,
would you snap out of it?

582
00:29:01.620 --> 00:29:04.710
I saw... a ghost...

583
00:29:04.790 --> 00:29:08.630
A ghost. A ghost...!

584
00:29:11.150 --> 00:29:12.810
Why are we...?

585
00:29:16.510 --> 00:29:20.350
– Hey.

586
00:29:19.030 --> 00:29:23.160
<b>God's Shrine</b>

587
00:29:23.400 --> 00:29:26.610
If you're gonna say
something, spit it out.

588
00:29:26.690 --> 00:29:29.650
Don't just stand there
chewing on your lip.

589
00:29:29.740 --> 00:29:31.450
Ah!

590
00:29:32.740 --> 00:29:35.950
Ah... Sorry.

591
00:29:36.030 --> 00:29:37.660
We all know why we're here,

592
00:29:37.740 --> 00:29:39.330
because you let Wyper
get away instead of

593
00:29:39.410 --> 00:29:41.210
killing him when
you had the chance.

594
00:29:41.290 --> 00:29:44.040
Now God Eneru will
punish us all for your failure!

595
00:29:47.400 --> 00:29:49.650
You think you're pretty
hot stuff since you got lucky

596
00:29:49.740 --> 00:29:52.610
and beat that fool Gan Fall,
don't you, Shura?

597
00:29:53.150 --> 00:29:54.810
Amusing.

598
00:29:59.950 --> 00:30:01.250
Your Majesty.

599
00:30:01.300 --> 00:30:02.000
Your priests have arrived.

600
00:30:02.000 --> 00:30:05.170
Very well. Open the gate.

601
00:30:15.170 --> 00:30:16.630
Not again.

602
00:30:16.720 --> 00:30:18.140
What are you doing?

603
00:30:18.220 --> 00:30:19.640
This is disgraceful!

604
00:30:20.720 --> 00:30:23.770
You should be ashamed!

605
00:30:23.850 --> 00:30:24.980
Shut up!

606
00:30:25.060 --> 00:30:27.770
These two have held
me back far too long!

607
00:30:27.860 --> 00:30:29.180
Just let me unleash
my full power!

608
00:30:29.180 --> 00:30:31.520
I could take care of
this whole island myself if it

609
00:30:31.600 --> 00:30:35.480
weren't for these two bunglers
always getting in my way!

610
00:30:35.570 --> 00:30:38.610
Hah! That's some
big talk, Shura.

611
00:30:38.690 --> 00:30:41.110
Maybe it's time for me to teach
you what the true meaning

612
00:30:41.200 --> 00:30:44.700
of power is if ya think
you've got the guts.

613
00:30:48.870 --> 00:30:53.830
Let's see if you can handle,
heh, the Ordeal of Iron.

614
00:30:53.850 --> 00:30:55.350
Your Ordeal of
Iron couldn't even

615
00:30:55.430 --> 00:30:57.230
test the strength of a child!

616
00:30:59.230 --> 00:31:02.820
My Ordeal of Swamp
is the ultimate challenge!

617
00:31:02.900 --> 00:31:05.860
Try that if you're
not too afraid!

618
00:31:05.950 --> 00:31:08.700
My Lord Gedatsu,
that looks extremely tiring.

619
00:31:08.780 --> 00:31:11.160
If you want to cross your arms
you need to hold them like this

620
00:31:11.240 --> 00:31:12.950
and rest them on your chest.

621
00:31:13.070 --> 00:31:14.440
Ah! Hey!

622
00:31:14.530 --> 00:31:17.320
Enough! Cease this chatter!

623
00:31:17.310 --> 00:31:19.940
<b>Yama
Skypiean Abbot</b>

624
00:31:17.410 --> 00:31:19.990
You're standing in the
presence of God himself!

625
00:31:20.080 --> 00:31:23.120
Really? I see an empty chair.

626
00:31:23.200 --> 00:31:25.410
I don't see
anyone sitting in it!

627
00:31:26.740 --> 00:31:28.320
Surprise, boys!

628
00:31:45.130 --> 00:31:46.420
You asked?

629
00:31:46.510 --> 00:31:47.720
Here I am.

630
00:31:47.680 --> 00:31:55.180
<b>Skypiea's One and Only
God Enel</b>

631
00:31:47.800 --> 00:31:50.760
You boys are getting slow.

632
00:31:50.850 --> 00:31:52.060
You're out of practice.

633
00:31:52.140 --> 00:31:54.480
If that pathetic display
is any indication,

634
00:31:54.560 --> 00:31:56.520
you're all well on your
way toward ending up

635
00:31:56.600 --> 00:31:58.440
dismal failures like Satori.

636
00:31:58.530 --> 00:32:01.570
What is the meaning of this?

637
00:32:01.730 --> 00:32:03.070
Why, God?

638
00:32:03.120 --> 00:32:04.250
Why do you mock us?

639
00:32:04.280 --> 00:32:06.200
Is that the reason
you summoned us here?

640
00:32:06.290 --> 00:32:08.040
To entertain yourself?

641
00:32:08.120 --> 00:32:09.450
I was bored.

642
00:32:11.830 --> 00:32:13.290
Now have a seat.

643
00:32:13.680 --> 00:32:15.390
You don't seem to have
given too much thought

644
00:32:15.460 --> 00:32:18.130
to the Blue Sea
dwellers yet, have you?

645
00:32:18.210 --> 00:32:21.300
God Eneru, if this
is about Satori's failure.

646
00:32:21.380 --> 00:32:23.510
That idiot
was too inexperienced.

647
00:32:23.590 --> 00:32:27.890
And that ridiculous
Ordeal of Spheres! Ha!

648
00:32:27.970 --> 00:32:32.350
You're hardly in
a position to talk, Shura.

649
00:32:33.240 --> 00:32:35.620
Why, they are looking for gold.

650
00:32:35.700 --> 00:32:37.490
That's obvious.

651
00:32:37.580 --> 00:32:39.160
What, gold?

652
00:32:39.240 --> 00:32:41.160
Impossible. How?

653
00:32:41.250 --> 00:32:42.960
How did they know?

654
00:32:43.040 --> 00:32:46.500
This island was
originally part of the Blue Sea.

655
00:32:46.580 --> 00:32:49.300
It's not so odd that they
should know about it.

656
00:32:52.840 --> 00:32:55.260
Of course,
they'll move tomorrow.

657
00:32:55.340 --> 00:32:57.220
As will the Shandorians.

658
00:32:58.420 --> 00:33:00.460
The rules state that
you each run an area of

659
00:33:00.550 --> 00:33:02.720
the Upper Yard, and you're
not allowed to enter

660
00:33:02.810 --> 00:33:07.140
each other's areas or interfere
with one another in any way.

661
00:33:07.230 --> 00:33:10.480
Tomorrow, I'll allow you
to go where you will.

662
00:33:10.640 --> 00:33:13.470
You may set up your
ordeals wherever you want.

663
00:33:14.400 --> 00:33:16.400
There will be no restrictions.

664
00:33:16.480 --> 00:33:18.900
Get as vicious as you like.

665
00:33:18.980 --> 00:33:21.570
Why are you being
so generous all of a sudden?

666
00:33:21.660 --> 00:33:23.160
Because, my friends.

667
00:33:23.240 --> 00:33:27.210
I am pleased to announce that
the Maxim is almost complete.

668
00:33:27.290 --> 00:33:28.960
So it's time
for us to put an end to

669
00:33:29.040 --> 00:33:31.630
this wretched island and
set forth on our journey

670
00:33:31.710 --> 00:33:33.960
to the world of dreams!

671
00:33:36.100 --> 00:33:39.140
It's true! I wasn't dreaming!

672
00:33:39.230 --> 00:33:41.120
Someone was here last night!

673
00:33:41.120 --> 00:33:42.790
– The Going Merry!
– The Going Merry!

674
00:33:42.880 --> 00:33:44.920
She's been repaired!

675
00:33:45.920 --> 00:33:47.710
I knew it!

676
00:33:48.280 --> 00:33:50.860
See, guys?
I told you I wasn't insane!

677
00:33:53.740 --> 00:33:55.240
I don't believe it.

678
00:33:55.330 --> 00:33:56.740
The mast is fixed.

679
00:33:56.830 --> 00:33:57.710
Hey, now that's service!

680
00:33:57.710 --> 00:34:02.380
Well, I hate to say it,
but they did a lousy job.

681
00:34:02.460 --> 00:34:04.470
Well, whoever
did it sure is nice!

682
00:34:04.470 --> 00:34:06.850
But who'd risk crossing a
river full of skysharks to come

683
00:34:06.930 --> 00:34:10.220
all the way out here
and fix our ship for us?

684
00:34:10.310 --> 00:34:13.020
I mean, as far as we
can tell, the only people here

685
00:34:13.100 --> 00:34:15.730
on Upper Yard are
us and our enemies.

686
00:34:15.810 --> 00:34:18.270
Hey, did you notice
they took all the flying gear

687
00:34:18.360 --> 00:34:21.190
off the ship? That's weird.

688
00:34:21.280 --> 00:34:24.700
Hmm... Yeah,
I been thinking about it,

689
00:34:24.780 --> 00:34:26.660
and it's really
got me wondering.

690
00:34:30.490 --> 00:34:33.370
Huh. It just doesn't
make any sense to me.

691
00:34:33.460 --> 00:34:35.830
How could this phantom repairman
know what the Merry's supposed

692
00:34:35.920 --> 00:34:37.670
to look like?

693
00:34:37.750 --> 00:34:39.550
How'd he know she
didn't always have a comb,

694
00:34:39.630 --> 00:34:42.630
or wings, or a tail?

695
00:34:43.080 --> 00:34:47.250
Hmm... How could
he possibly have known?

696
00:34:52.300 --> 00:34:56.390
C'mon, Merry,
just tell me who I saw.

697
00:35:00.220 --> 00:35:02.310
Okay, let's look at the map.

698
00:35:02.330 --> 00:35:06.040
The exploration team will be
taking this route moving south.

699
00:35:06.730 --> 00:35:08.190
There should be
some old ruins near

700
00:35:08.270 --> 00:35:09.690
the skull's right eye.

701
00:35:09.750 --> 00:35:13.050
Keep an eye out for enemies
and bring back that gold!

702
00:35:13.050 --> 00:35:14.880
Heh. You make it sound so easy.

703
00:35:15.000 --> 00:35:17.050
Hold on, you're the one
who keeps talking about gold

704
00:35:17.130 --> 00:35:18.880
and more gold,
but you're not coming?

705
00:35:18.960 --> 00:35:21.340
Well, of course not...
it's way too scary!

706
00:35:21.420 --> 00:35:22.680
She wants the gold,

707
00:35:22.760 --> 00:35:24.800
but she doesn't want
to risk anything to get it?

708
00:35:24.890 --> 00:35:26.620
That's just too weird!

709
00:35:26.620 --> 00:35:28.830
We'll be in danger,
too, you know.

710
00:35:28.920 --> 00:35:32.590
We'll be taking the Merry
down river through the island.

711
00:35:32.670 --> 00:35:35.050
Then, we'll head for
the beach near the ruins

712
00:35:35.450 --> 00:35:37.320
We can meet up here.

713
00:35:37.320 --> 00:35:39.780
And then we can escape
this stupid sky island!

714
00:35:40.570 --> 00:35:43.740
At long last, we'll be a rich
and powerful pirate crew!

715
00:35:43.820 --> 00:35:45.200
Able to buy anything!

716
00:35:45.280 --> 00:35:48.530
Oh, yeah!
All the meat I can eat!

717
00:35:48.620 --> 00:35:49.950
Escape. That sounds great!

718
00:35:49.950 --> 00:35:51.780
Just don't make me the bait!

719
00:35:52.590 --> 00:35:55.090
Look! The weather's perfect!

720
00:35:55.090 --> 00:35:56.590
Sure, we're
on top of the clouds.

721
00:35:56.870 --> 00:35:59.450
Okay! We'll all meet
safely on the east coast!

722
00:36:00.350 --> 00:36:01.680
– You bet!
– Let's get going, then!

723
00:36:01.680 --> 00:36:02.970
Yeah!

724
00:36:33.990 --> 00:36:36.870
Who will fall
before my Ordeal of String?

725
00:36:36.950 --> 00:36:40.500
The Shandorians or
the Blue Sea dwellers?

726
00:36:41.170 --> 00:36:43.800
And so the festival begins.

727
00:36:48.920 --> 00:36:52.720
Magnificent.
Today will be a great day.
